# Where a line's time goes: the checker answers an error, the toolchain a value.
Shot fast-errors
Alt :time on, then a call built and run by the real toolchain in about a third of a second, and the same call missing an argument, answered by the in-process type checker in about a millisecond
Caption A type error comes back in a millisecond: gluon type-checks in process before it builds. A line that runs pays for the real compiler — and gets the compiler's semantics.
